# Cursor Config Lookup

## Local-first lookup order

When the question is about Cursor behavior or this `.cursor` folder, search in this order:

1. `.cursor/README.md`
2. `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`
3. `.cursor/skills/**/SKILL.md` plus supporting checklists/templates/resources
4. `.cursor/agents/*.md`
5. `.cursor/hooks.json` and `.cursor/hooks/**`
6. `.cursor/mcp.json`
7. `.cursor/commands/*.md` if present
8. `.cursor/workflows/*.md` as reference only
9. `.cursor/scripts/*` when behavior is implemented in code rather than prose

## Use

Use this rule to locate the governing Cursor surface before answering configuration questions. Keep answers grounded in file paths and avoid treating archived compatibility files as active runtime behavior.

**Local Qwen vLLM Docker boot:** [`docs/cursor/briefing_local_qwen_docker_boot_20260526.md`](../../docs/cursor/briefing_local_qwen_docker_boot_20260526.md) (one-pager) · [`docs/cursor/local_qwen_docker_boot.md`](../../docs/cursor/local_qwen_docker_boot.md) (full runbook).

## Archive boundary

`.cursor/cursor_compat/**`, `.cursor/_zero_loss_originals/**`, `.cursor/scripts/_legacy_cursor/**`, and `.cursor/plans/_archive/**` are historical compatibility material unless a user explicitly asks for migration history.
